From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AztecBot <tech@aztec-labs.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 19:02:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(pxe): charge the teardown call's AVM startup gas in
 kernelless simulation

The AVM dispatches the teardown call like any other enqueued public call, so it consumes FIXED_AVM_STARTUP_L2_GAS on top of its gas limits. Charging it changes the private kernel's circuit, so the protocol gates it behind the 0/1 constant TEARDOWN_AVM_STARTUP_L2_GAS_ENABLED, which the private kernel's gas meter reads as well. Kernelless simulation is what gas estimation runs on, so it reads the same constant and adds the startup gas only when it is non-zero: otherwise the estimated gas limits of a tx with a teardown call would differ from the gas_used the kernel proves, and a tx estimated too low would be rejected for exceeding its limits.

diff --git a/yarn-project/pxe/src/contract_function_simulator/contract_function_simulator.ts b/yarn-project/pxe/src/contract_function_simulator/contract_function_simulator.ts
index 687ba34a4fae9118b98496fffde9c7fec71e56b3..4c2e4ce85c2cea848f706671df58594328db9036 100644
--- a/yarn-project/pxe/src/contract_function_simulator/contract_function_simulator.ts
+++ b/yarn-project/pxe/src/contract_function_simulator/contract_function_simulator.ts
@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@ import {
   PRIVATE_TX_L2_GAS_OVERHEAD,
   PUBLIC_DATA_WRITE_LENGTH,
   PUBLIC_TX_L2_GAS_OVERHEAD,
+  TEARDOWN_AVM_STARTUP_L2_GAS_ENABLED,
   TX_DA_GAS_OVERHEAD,
 } from '@aztec-labs/constants';
 import { arrayNonEmptyLength, padArrayEnd } from '@aztec-labs/foundation/collection';
@@ -732,7 +733,16 @@ export async function generateSimulatedProvingResult(
     );
     gasUsed = meterGasUsed(revertibleData, isPrivateOnlyTx).add(meterGasUsed(nonRevertibleData, isPrivateOnlyTx));
     if (publicTeardownCallRequest) {
-      gasUsed = gasUsed.add(privateExecutionResult.entrypoint.publicInputs.txContext.gasSettings.teardownGasLimits);
+      // The teardown call is dispatched by the AVM like any other enqueued public call, so it consumes the startup
+      // gas on top of its gas limits. Whether it is charged is a 0/1 protocol constant that the private kernel's gas
+      // meter reads too, so both meter the same amount.
+      const teardownStartupGas = Gas.from({
+        daGas: 0,
+        l2Gas: FIXED_AVM_STARTUP_L2_GAS * TEARDOWN_AVM_STARTUP_L2_GAS_ENABLED,
+      });
+      gasUsed = gasUsed
+        .add(privateExecutionResult.entrypoint.publicInputs.txContext.gasSettings.teardownGasLimits)
+        .add(teardownStartupGas);
     }
 
     inputsForPublic = new PartialPrivateTailPublicInputsForPublic(
